Hoist close's pending worklist onto Structure

Structure now owns a `pending_equalities: Vec<(ElId, ElId)>`. equate()
just pushes onto it and takes no conflicts argument. The local loop
inside the old union_eagerly moved into a drain_equalities pass that
close() invokes as part of its fixed point.

functionality and impose_concrete_type no longer call out to
union_eagerly; they enqueue pairs on pending_equalities and trust the
next drain pass to apply them. The close fixed point becomes:
drain -> functionality -> typing, looping until all three report no
work. On exit pending_equalities is empty.

Rationale: every equivalence class has at most one ConcreteType, so
declaring two elements equal forces their parent lists to reconcile
pointwise. The pending list is the natural queue for that cascade;
owning it on Structure means equate() is trivial and all conflict
reporting surfaces in one place inside close().

Previous commits on this branch: Structure, algebraize and the initial
close pass.
